:"text","text":", my eight-year-old brother, and "},{"type":"text","text":"I"},{"type":"text","text":" unwillingly said good-bye to all of our friends. "},{"type":"text","text":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"ho knew if we"},{"type":"text","text":"’"},{"type":"text","text":"d ever see them again? "},{"type":"text","text":"F"},{"type":"text","text":"inally, the "},{"type":"text","text":"moment"},{"type":"text","text":" of our departure arrived, and we loaded suitcases, books, games, "},{"type":"text","text":"camping ","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":"equipment, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" tent","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":" into the car and bravely drove off. "},{"type":"text","text":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"e bravely drove off again two hours later after we"},{"type":"text","text":"’"},{"type":"text","text":"d "},{"type":"text","text":"returned"},{"type":"text","text":" home to get the purse and traveler"},{"type":"text","text":"’"},{"type":"text","text":"s checks "},{"type":"text","text":"Mom","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":" had forgotten."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"D"},{"type":"text","text":"avid and "},{"type":"text","text":"I"},{"type":"text","text":" were always a little nervous when using gas station bathrooms if Mom was driving while "},{"type":"text","text":"Dad","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":" slept: "},{"type":"text","text":"“"},{"type":"text","text":"You stand "},{"type":"text","text":"outside"},{"type":"text","text":" the door and play lookout("},{"type":"text","text":"放哨"},{"type":"text","text":") while "},{"type":"text","text":"I"},{"type":"text","text":" go, and "},{"type":"text","text":"I’"},{"type":"text","text":"ll stand "},{"type":"text","text":"outside"},{"type":"text","text":" the door and play lookout while you go."},{"type":"text","text":"”"},{"type":"text","text":"I"},{"type":"text","text":" had terrible pictures in my mind: "},{"type":"text","text":"“"},{"type":"text","text":"Honey, where are the kids?"},{"type":"text","text":"”"},{"type":"text","text":"“"},{"type":"text","text":"What?! Oh, Gos"},{"type":"text","text":"h…"},{"type":"text","text":"I thought "},{"type":"text","text":"they were being awfully quiet."},{"type":"text","text":"”"},{"type":"text","text":" We were never actually left behind in a strange city, but we weren"},{"type":"text","text":"’"},{"type":"text","text":"t about to take any chances."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"O"},{"type":"text","text":"n "},{"type":"text","text":"the"},{"type":"text","text":" fourth or fifth night, we had "},{"type":"text","text":"trouble","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":" finding a hotel with a vacancy. "},{"type":"text","text":"A"},{"type":"text","text":"fter driving in vain for some time, Mom suddenly got a great idea: Why didn"},{"type":"text","text":"’"},{"type":"text","text":"t we find a house with a likely-looking backyard and ask if we could set up tent there? David and "},{"type":"text","text":"I"},{"type":"text","text":" became nervous. "},{"type":"text","text":"T"},{"type":"text","text":"o our great relief, Dad turned down the idea. "},{"type":"text","text":"M"},{"type":"text","text":"om never could understand our objections("},{"type":"text","text":"反对"},{"type":"text","text":"). If a strange "},{"type":"text","text":"family"},{"type":"text","text":" showed up on her front doorstep, Mom would have been delighted. She thinks everyone in the world is as "},{"type":"text","text":"nice","underline":true},{"type":"text","text":" as she is. "},{"type":"text","text":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"e "},{"type":"text","text":"finally"},{"type":"text","text":" found a vacancy in the next town."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"注意："}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"1."},{"type":"text","text":"所续写短文的词数应为"},{"type":"text","text":"150"},{"type":"text","text":"左右；"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"2."},{"type":"text","text":"至少使用"},{"type":"text","text":"5"},{"type":"text","text":"个短文中标有下划线的关键词语；"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"3."},{"type":"text","text":"续写部分分为两段，每段的开头已为你写好；"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"4."},{"type":"text","text":"续写完成后，请用下划线标出你所使用的关键词语。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Para1:  "},{"type":"text","text":"The next day we remembered the brand-new tent we had brought with us."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Para2:  "},{"type":"text","text":"We drove through several states and saw lots of great sights along the way."}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"none","gradingMode":"none","kind":"none"},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"583db154db8703ae6b42925aa367070712a82869dfd19f3f893208b6107c0716","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2017年高考英语试卷（浙江）（11月）听力音频.mp3","sha256":"583db154db8703ae6b42925aa367070712a82869dfd19f3f893208b6107c0716","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"media-manifest","confidence":0.9},{"sourceDocumentId":"fdaa93d18e64494cdd39aeaf5426789234239a01c7f3e0f4609f81d627da940f","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2017年高考英语试卷（浙江）（11月）（空白卷）.doc","sha256":"fdaa93d18e64494cdd39aeaf5426789234239a01c7f3e0f4609f81d627da940f","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.9},{"sourceDocumentId":"11aa3a75a1aad6e4a9eaf450141d744be96894f2966b09b974907b36188709d5","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2017年高考英语试卷（浙江）（11月）（解析卷）.doc","sha256":"11aa3a75a1aad6e4a9eaf450141d744be96894f2966b09b974907b36188709d5","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.9}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"3fdfe858d4a4a046912a3064b244a778fb8596a8ee6c55be1e3ece26def396a0"}}],"title":"浙江省2017年11月新高考英语试题","presentation":"writing"},{"id":"continuation-writing-paper-2019-zhejiang-regional-june-section-5-group-5-2-group","instructions":[],"stimulusBlocks":[],"sharedOptions":[],"questions":[{"id":"continuation-writing-paper-2019-zhejiang-regional-june-section-5-group-5-2-q-61","displayNumber":2,"sourceQuestionNumber":102,"type":"essay","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"67."},{"type":"text","text":"阅读下面短文，根据其内容写一篇"},{"type":"text","text":"60"},{"type":"text","text":"词左右的内容概要。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Parents everywhere praise their kids. Jenn Berman, author of The A to Z Guide to Raising Happy and Confident Kids, says, \"We've gone to the opposite extreme of a few decades ago when parents tended to be more strict.\" By giving kids a lot of praise, parents think they're building their children's confidence, when, in fact, it may be just the opposite. Too much praise can backfire and, when given in a way that's insincere, make kids afraid to try new things or take a risk for fear of not being able to stay on top where their parents' praise has put them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Still, don't go too far in the other direction. Not giving enough praise can be just as damaging gas giving too much. Kids will feel like they're not good enough or that you don't care and, as a result, may see no point in trying hard for their accomplishments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"So what is the right amount of praise? Experts say that the quality of praise is more important than the quantity. If praise is sincere and focused on the effort not the outcome, you can give it as often as your child does something that deserves a verbal reward.\" We should especially recognize our children's efforts to push themselves and work hard to achieve a goal, \"says Donahue, author of Parenting Without Fear: Letting Go of Worry and Focusing on What Really Matters. \"One thing to remember is that it's the process not the end product that matters.\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Your son may not be the best basketball player on his team. But if he's out there every day and playing hard, you should praise his effort regardless of whether his team wins or loses. Praising the effort and not the outcome can also mean recognizing your child when she has worked hard to clean the yard, cook dinner, or finish a book report. But whatever it is, praise should be given on a case-by-case basis and be proportionate("},{"type":"text","text":"相称的"},{"type":"text","text":")to the amount of effort your child has put into it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"none","gradingMode":"none","kind":"none"},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"4c8aded6b2a7b39ad2f0c4ab7d8b48e83274715aa4cbe4a840b87fcd5bc4d9da","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2019年高考英语试卷（浙江）（6月）听力音频.mp3","sha256":"4c8aded6b2a7b39ad2f0c4ab7d8b48e83274715aa4cbe4a840b87fcd5bc4d9da","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"media-manifest","confidence":0.9},{"sourceDocumentId":"e1920cc987f319c118661a2b36fdd844bff5ede41ff62f584ff5b5fc8b69186f","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2019年高考英语试卷（浙江）（6月）（空白卷）.doc","sha256":"e1920cc987f319c118661a2b36fdd844bff5ede41ff62f584ff5b5fc8b69186f","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.9},{"sourceDocumentId":"87dd1d3806304d80b1e30690cd1bf4d75de824c53f0ebc634b36747106782238","relativePath":"历年真题/【未上传】2019年高考英语试卷（浙江）（6月）（解析卷）.doc","sha256":"87dd1d3806304d80b1e30690cd1bf4d75de824c53f0ebc634b36747106782238","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.9}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"108c6573929aef46bc6af83cbac